IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ml52-nouns`
IMPORT `ml52-cross-references`

-- Row il-52. The two controls hold, and the recorded facts about the two defects are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their four failing assertions are in ml52-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in ml52-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound controls`

-- Control 1: the order's two items bear different labels, and every label names one item on the days before the Act's item starts.
#ASSERT NOT `two items are certainly read on the day and bear one label` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (`item: second item of the 2026 order, label (18י)`) (Date 1 3 2028)
#ASSERT `the labels are distinct on` (Date 1 12 2026)
#ASSERT `the labels are distinct on` (Date 26 1 2028)
-- Control 2: the order of 2016 puts item (18ו) where it says, and the consolidation prints the place as in force.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the place after item (18ה), where the 2016 order puts item (18ו)`)
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: the place after item (18ה), where the 2016 order puts item (18ו)`)

§ `Tests of what the numbering records say`

-- Before the order's first day (the editor's reading) nothing is read; from it, both items are certainly read well inside the two years.
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (Date 8 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (Date 9 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: second item of the 2026 order, label (18י)`) (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- From the first day the order's items could be over, the sources held do not say: NOTHING (fork P1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (Date 7 6 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (Date 8 6 2028) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Act's item: not read the day before 27 January 2028 (as enacted), read from that day, with no end in the instrument.
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`) (Date 26 1 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`) (Date 27 1 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the item is certainly read on` (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`) (Date 10 11 2040) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Where the labels meet: one (18ט) before the Act's item starts, two from the day it starts while the order's items are certainly read, one (18י) throughout.
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18ט)" (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18ט)" (Date 26 1 2028) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18ט)" (Date 27 1 2028) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18ט)" (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18י)" (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `two recorded items bearing one label are certainly read on` (Date 27 1 2028)
-- After the order's items could be over, the row does not say: the count falls to one only because NOTHING is not counted.
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18ט)" (Date 8 6 2028) EQUALS 1

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No reference here has both limbs read from the official instruments alone.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: the place after item (18ה), where the 2016 order puts item (18ו)`))
-- Defect 2: limb (a), the lapse, is the consolidation only; limb (b) carries the caveat.
#ASSERT (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Defect 1: the order's first day is the editor's reading (the consolidation only); its length is read from the page image.
#ASSERT (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`)'s `the first day was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`)'s `the length was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
-- The Act's item: both readings carry the caveat that no postponement order was looked for.
#ASSERT (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`)'s `the first day was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

§ `Tests of what the descriptions of defect 2 say`

#ASSERT (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `section 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law, in force while the 2013 temporary law brings it in`
#ASSERT (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `section 7ג of the Infiltration Law as its consolidation prints it, with a lapse marker in place of text`
-- The consolidation prints the named text as lapsed (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY).
#ASSERT (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)'s `the consolidation prints the named text as lapsed` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)

§ `Tests of the day the named text stopped being in force`

-- The day the period ended was not established, so the answer is NOTHING on every day, and a control has no recorded end either (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`) (Date 1 1 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`) (Date 27 9 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: the place after item (18ה), where the 2016 order puts item (18ו)`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
